---A reference to data stored on the filesystem, on GFS or in blobstore.
---@class gcp.walletobjects_v1.Media
---@field diffDownloadResponse? gcp.walletobjects_v1.DiffDownloadResponse Set if reference_type is DIFF_DOWNLOAD_RESPONSE.
---@field isPotentialRetry? boolean |is_potential_retry| is set false only when Scotty is certain that it has not sent the request before. When a client resumes an upload, this field must be set true in agent calls, because Scotty cannot be certain that it has never sent the request before due to potential failure in the session state persistence.
---@field timestamp? string Time at which the media data was last updated, in milliseconds since UNIX epoch
---@field cosmoBinaryReference? string A binary data reference for a media download. Serves as a technology-agnostic binary reference in some Google infrastructure. This value is a serialized storage_cosmo.BinaryReference proto. Storing it as bytes is a hack to get around the fact that the cosmo proto (as well as others it includes) doesn't support JavaScript. This prevents us from including the actual type of this field.
---@field crc32cHash? number For Scotty Uploads: Scotty-provided hashes for uploads For Scotty Downloads: (WARNING: DO NOT USE WITHOUT PERMISSION FROM THE SCOTTY TEAM.) A Hash provided by the agent to be used to verify the data being downloaded. Currently only supported for inline payloads. Further, only crc32c_hash is currently supported.
---@field diffChecksumsResponse? gcp.walletobjects_v1.DiffChecksumsResponse Set if reference_type is DIFF_CHECKSUMS_RESPONSE.
---@field compositeMedia? gcp.walletobjects_v1.CompositeMediaList A composite media composed of one or more media objects, set if reference_type is COMPOSITE_MEDIA. The media length field must be set to the sum of the lengths of all composite media objects. Note: All composite media must have length specified.
---@field sha512Hash? string Scotty-provided SHA512 hash for an upload.
---@field diffUploadRequest? gcp.walletobjects_v1.DiffUploadRequest Set if reference_type is DIFF_UPLOAD_REQUEST.
---@field hash? string Deprecated, use one of explicit hash type fields instead. These two hash related fields will only be populated on Scotty based media uploads and will contain the content of the hash group in the NotificationRequest: http://cs/#google3/blobstore2/api/scotty/service/proto/upload_listener.proto&q=class:Hash Hex encoded hash value of the uploaded media.
---@field referenceType? gcp.walletobjects_v1.MediaReferenceTypeEnum|string Describes what the field reference contains.
---@field mediaId? string Media id to forward to the operation GetMedia. Can be set if reference_type is GET_MEDIA.
---@field algorithm? string Deprecated, use one of explicit hash type fields instead. Algorithm used for calculating the hash. As of 2011/01/21, "MD5" is the only possible value for this field. New values may be added at any time.
---@field md5Hash? string Scotty-provided MD5 hash for an upload.
---@field bigstoreObjectRef? string Use object_id instead.
---@field length? string Size of the data, in bytes
---@field diffUploadResponse? gcp.walletobjects_v1.DiffUploadResponse Set if reference_type is DIFF_UPLOAD_RESPONSE.
---@field sha256Hash? string Scotty-provided SHA256 hash for an upload.
---@field hashVerified? boolean For Scotty uploads only. If a user sends a hash code and the backend has requested that Scotty verify the upload against the client hash, Scotty will perform the check on behalf of the backend and will reject it if the hashes don't match. This is set to true if Scotty performed this verification.
---@field contentTypeInfo? gcp.walletobjects_v1.ContentTypeInfo Extended content type information provided for Scotty uploads.
---@field filename? string Original file name
---@field diffVersionResponse? gcp.walletobjects_v1.DiffVersionResponse Set if reference_type is DIFF_VERSION_RESPONSE.
---@field objectId? gcp.walletobjects_v1.ObjectId Reference to a TI Blob, set if reference_type is BIGSTORE_REF.
---@field blobstore2Info? gcp.walletobjects_v1.Blobstore2Info Blobstore v2 info, set if reference_type is BLOBSTORE_REF and it refers to a v2 blob.
---@field token? string A unique fingerprint/version id for the media data
---@field path? string Path to the data, set if reference_type is PATH
---@field contentType? string MIME type of the data
---@field sha1Hash? string Scotty-provided SHA1 hash for an upload.
---@field inline? string Media data, set if reference_type is INLINE
---@field downloadParameters? gcp.walletobjects_v1.DownloadParameters Parameters for a media download.
---@field blobRef? string Blobstore v1 reference, set if reference_type is BLOBSTORE_REF This should be the byte representation of a blobstore.BlobRef. Since Blobstore is deprecating v1, use blobstore2_info instead. For now, any v2 blob will also be represented in this field as v1 BlobRef.

---@alias gcp.walletobjects_v1.MediaReferenceTypeEnum "PATH"|"BLOB_REF"|"INLINE"|"GET_MEDIA"|"COMPOSITE_MEDIA"|"BIGSTORE_REF"|"DIFF_VERSION_RESPONSE"|"DIFF_CHECKSUMS_RESPONSE"|"DIFF_DOWNLOAD_RESPONSE"|"DIFF_UPLOAD_REQUEST"|"DIFF_UPLOAD_RESPONSE"|"COSMO_BINARY_REFERENCE"|"ARBITRARY_BYTES"

---Extra information added to operations that support Scotty media requests.
---@class gcp.walletobjects_v1.MediaRequestInfo
---@field notificationType? gcp.walletobjects_v1.MediaRequestInfoNotificationTypeEnum|string The type of notification received from Scotty.
---@field requestId? string The Scotty request ID.
---@field diffObjectVersion? string Set if the http request info is diff encoded. The value of this field is the version number of the base revision. This is corresponding to Apiary's mediaDiffObjectVersion (//depot/google3/java/com/google/api/server/media/variable/DiffObjectVersionVariable.java). See go/esf-scotty-diff-upload for more information.
---@field physicalHeaders? string The physical headers provided by RequestReceivedParameters in Scotty request. type is uploader_service.KeyValuePairs.
---@field totalBytesIsEstimated? boolean Whether the total bytes field contains an estimated data.
---@field requestReceivedParamsServingInfo? string The partition of the Scotty server handling this request. type is uploader_service.RequestReceivedParamsServingInfo LINT.IfChange(request_received_params_serving_info_annotations) LINT.ThenChange()
---@field customData? string Data to be copied to backend requests. Custom data is returned to Scotty in the agent_state field, which Scotty will then provide in subsequent upload notifications.
---@field currentBytes? string The number of current bytes uploaded or downloaded.
---@field finalStatus? number The existence of the final_status field indicates that this is the last call to the agent for this request_id. http://google3/uploader/agent/scotty_agent.proto?l=737&rcl=347601929
---@field totalBytes? string The total size of the file.

---@alias gcp.walletobjects_v1.MediaRequestInfoNotificationTypeEnum "START"|"PROGRESS"|"END"|"RESPONSE_SENT"|"ERROR"

